  "parts": [
    {
      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "Find all of the subsets of $U=\\{-\\pi ,\\pi \\}.$",
      "original_html_sha256": "7216ce9810f157ce2730c2634f0522d2ab088ce61f10474590cda5aa911371c2",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/7216ce9810f157ce2730c2634f0522d2ab088ce61f10474590cda5aa911371c2.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    },
    {
      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "To find every subset of $U,$ we list out every combination of elements within $U.$ \n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/assets/b0e483a2d10cba17fb2bd3bf0e78d7b4d2fc07b22dbb5c492564b998bbfce6fc.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n∅,\\{-\\pi \\},\\{\\pi \\},\\{-\\pi ,\\pi \\}.\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "02b9dfbbdd62a6fe55c4a76511a59959821d513cf983071c418cf23006130601",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
